<persname role="subject" source="lcnaf">Thompson, Harlan H. (Harlan Howard), 1894-1987. </persname></origination>
<physdesc label="Extent">
<extent>29 boxes (14.5 linear ft.)</extent>
<extent>3 oversize boxes.</extent>
</physdesc>
<abstract label="Abstract">Harlan Thompson was a writer of western novels for young people, sometimes published under the pseudonym, Stephen Holt; international president of P.E.N., 1958-59; won Boys' Clubs of America gold medal for <title>Prairie Colt</title> in 1948, and Commonwealth Club juvenile silver medal for <title>Spook</title>, <title>The Mustang</title> in 1957; other publications include <title>Wild Palomino</title> (1946), <title>Star Roan</title> (1952), and <title>Stormy</title> (1955). Collection consists of manuscripts and books by Thompson.</abstract>
<repository label="Repository">
<corpname source="lcnaf">University of California, Los Angeles. Library. Department of Special Collections.</corpname>
<address><addressline>Los Angeles, California 90095-1575</addressline></address>
</repository>
